      "content": "That makes sense, but it still feels like they're just using IP and liability as shields to block competition. I mean, if you look at how actual consumers experience it, they can't even get a basic screen fixed without it being overpriced. Do you think their arguments about \"brand reputation\" and \"trade secrets\" are actually valid protections, or are they just strategic ways to maintain a monopoly on the repair market?",
